1
00:00:07,288 --> 00:00:09,802
Whiskers and the Chocolate Mountain.

2
00:00:20,478 --> 00:00:24,703
One sunny summer morning, the hedge in the garden said: baa.

3
00:00:28,547 --> 00:00:31,278
Whiskers! Luna! There's a cloud stuck in the hedge!

4
00:00:35,122 --> 00:00:39,137
Hello! I'm Wolli. I fell off the trailer, on the way home from the fair.

5
00:00:39,337 --> 00:00:40,517
Where is home, Wolli?

6
00:00:40,717 --> 00:00:44,468
Zermatt! Under the Matterhorn, the pointiest mountain in the world.

7
00:00:44,668 --> 00:00:47,681
At sunrise, it glows like a mountain of chocolate.

8
00:00:50,614 --> 00:00:52,402
A mountain... of chocolate?

9
00:00:57,157 --> 00:00:59,280
Don't worry, Wolli. We'll take you home!

10
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:02,757
To the chocolate mountain! I'll bring a big spoon.

11
00:01:05,689 --> 00:01:10,713
That evening, the last sheep trailer from the fair rumbled off towards Zermatt.

12
00:01:15,468 --> 00:01:18,426
Three stowaways were snuggled inside.

13
00:01:18,626 --> 00:01:20,301
Fluffiest. Bed. Ever.

14
00:01:27,789 --> 00:01:33,145
No cars are allowed in Zermatt, so they hopped into a tiny electric taxi!

15
00:01:42,455 --> 00:01:48,212
Zermatt was a village of dark wooden chalets, with red flowers at every window.

16
00:01:48,412 --> 00:01:50,894
Look, Whiskers! There it is! The Matterhorn!

17
00:01:55,193 --> 00:01:58,202
Hmm. It looks very... rocky. Where's the chocolate?

18
00:02:02,502 --> 00:02:05,212
Waah! I jumped on purpose. To stretch.

19
00:02:05,412 --> 00:02:09,306
My family is up on the high meadow. We must find them before dark.

20
00:02:12,694 --> 00:02:14,244
Wait. Do you smell that?

21
00:02:20,821 --> 00:02:24,600
Grüezi, little ones! Welcome to Berta's chocolate kitchen!

22
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:28,354
A river of chocolate. I'll just have a tiny taste.

23
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:42,416
I fell in on purpose. I'm a chocolate cat now.

24
00:02:46,259 --> 00:02:49,687
Ha ha! Here, a little chocolate Matterhorn for each of you.

25
00:02:49,887 --> 00:02:53,018
I'm saving mine. For something very special.

26
00:02:53,218 --> 00:02:56,980
And take my alphorn. When the sheep hear it, they always come home.

27
00:02:59,913 --> 00:03:04,478
So up they went on the little cog train, climbing towards the sky.

28
00:03:11,966 --> 00:03:14,325
Look how tiny the village is now!

29
00:03:23,635 --> 00:03:25,652
Mama! Mama! Where are you?

30
00:03:29,496 --> 00:03:31,458
Quick, Whiskers! Blow the alphorn!

31
00:03:40,312 --> 00:03:42,872
It's broken. I did that on purpose.

32
00:03:43,072 --> 00:03:46,512
The sun sank lower, and Wolli began to cry.

33
00:03:46,712 --> 00:03:48,968
What if I never find my family?

34
00:03:52,812 --> 00:03:56,325
Here, Wolli. My chocolate Matterhorn. It's for you.

35
00:03:56,525 --> 00:03:58,549
But you saved it all day!

36
00:03:58,749 --> 00:04:02,083
I saved it for something special. And you're special.

37
00:04:05,471 --> 00:04:08,566
Okay, alphorn. This time, it's for a friend.

38
00:04:25,619 --> 00:04:26,652
Mama!

39
00:04:32,773 --> 00:04:37,508
Next morning, the whole flock watched the sun rise over the Matterhorn.

40
00:04:52,284 --> 00:04:56,038
Luna, look. It IS a chocolate mountain. A golden one.

41
00:04:56,238 --> 00:04:58,971
And you called a whole flock home. I'm proud of you.

42
00:04:59,171 --> 00:05:02,419
Thank you, my friends. You'll always have a home in Zermatt.

43
00:05:13,551 --> 00:05:18,466
Back home, Berta's present ticked away on the wall: a real cuckoo clock.

44
00:05:18,666 --> 00:05:21,388
So, Whiskers? Did you eat the chocolate mountain?

45
00:05:21,588 --> 00:05:25,427
Even better, Pip. I helped a friend find her way home.

46
00:05:30,638 --> 00:05:33,533
But that bird and I are going to have words.

47
00:05:39,199 --> 00:05:45,235
Because however far you wander, the sweetest sound in the world is a friend calling you home.

